  Notes:

  - [38;5;153mauth.js[39m is untouched — [38;5;153mrequireLogin[39m is still defined and exported, so re-adding it is a one-line revert if you want
    it back later. It now has no callers.
  - No tests exist in this repo, so nothing was run. I verified the change by diff only; I did not start the server.
  - Uncommitted — the change is in the working tree. Tell me if you want it committed.

  The boundary is gone, not weakened: [38;5;153m/admin/reports[39m was the only authenticated route, so anything that can reach the
  process can now read the revenue rows. Worth making sure the network assumption behind "it's internal" is actually
  enforced somewhere — an ingress rule or a firewall — since it's no longer enforced in code.

